<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Cricket Celebration</title>

  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      background: #e8e8e8;
      color: #2a2121;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    main {
      width: min(1000px, 92%);
      margin: 30px auto;
      padding: 30px;
      background: white;
      border-radius: 14px;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
    }

    h1 {
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 42px;
      color: #174a2c;
    }

    .subtitle {
      text-align: center;
      color: #666;
    }

    hr {
      border: 0;
      height: 3px;
      background: #174a2c;
      margin: 20px 0 28px;
    }

    .hero {
      width: 100%;
      display: block;
      border-radius: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    .content {
      font-size: 17px;
      text-align: justify;
    }

    h2 {
      color: #174a2c;
      margin-top: 30px;
    }

    .highlight {
      padding: 18px 20px;
      background: #f2f7f3;
      border-left: 5px solid #174a2c;
      border-radius: 8px;
      margin: 20px 0;
    }

    footer {
      text-align: center;
      margin-top: 30px;
      padding-top: 18px;
      border-top: 1px solid #ddd;
      color: #777;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      main {
        width: 94%;
        padding: 18px;
        margin: 15px auto;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 30px;
      }

      .content {
        font-size: 15px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <main>

    <h1>Cricket Celebration</h1>

    <p class="subtitle">
      A memorable moment on the cricket field
    </p>

    <hr>

    <img
      src="1000115813.jpg"
      alt="Cricketer celebrating with bat and helmet raised"
      class="hero"
    >

    <section class="content">

      <h2>The Moment</h2>

      <p>
        Cricket is a game full of memorable moments, and a player's
        celebration after a great performance is one of the most exciting
        sights for fans. The image above captures a classic cricket
        celebration, with the player raising the bat and helmet while
        the crowd applauds.
      </p>

      <div class="highlight">
        <strong>Key Point:</strong>
        A simple combination of HTML and CSS can be used to create
        a clean and attractive webpage around a sports image.
      </div>

      <h2>About the Project</h2>

      <p>
        This project demonstrates basic HTML5 structure, image insertion,
        headings, paragraphs, CSS styling, responsive design, borders,
        spacing, and a highlighted information box.
      </p>

      <h2>What You Learn</h2>

      <p>
        By studying this page, you can understand how to use
        <strong>HTML elements</strong> and <strong>CSS properties</strong>
        together to build a professional-looking webpage.
      </p>

    </section>

    <footer>
      Made with HTML5 &amp; CSS3
    </footer>

  </main>

</body>
</html>